 ## Color
-- Build from roles (ink, surface, accent, status), not from a brand-color-everywhere approach.
-- Neutrals carry 80–90% of the surface. Accent is rare enough to mean something.
+- Build from the token plan's roles (action, status, data marks, signature, text, surface, focus), not from a brand-color-everywhere approach.
+- Neutrals carry 80–90% of the surface. The accent is the action color: it goes only on things you press and on the item currently selected in a set (the open tab, the one chosen option). It never marks data or a state (switched on, done, pending, available, failed), and never decorates (a rule, a band, a highlighted word, the logo).
+- The focus ring is a color that reaches 3:1 on every surface it lands on; it may be the action color if that holds.
 - Tint neutrals slightly toward the accent hue rather than using pure gray.
 - Status colors (success, warning, danger) are reserved for status.
 - Dark mode is its own palette: raise surface lightness for elevation, desaturate accents, never pure #000 with pure #FFF body text for long reading.
