+- **Accent**: name three candidates from the subject, at least 90° apart in hue or very different in chroma (a muted ink, a saturated signal, a near-neutral), each with its source. The accent is the action color: it marks only what the user presses and the item currently selected, so choose the candidate that is free to mean just "press this". Status colors and the signature's color are separate roles with their own lines in the plan (§4): a hue that already means a state in the subject, or that the signature is made of, stays in that role, however neatly a metaphor ties it to the button. Write one line on why not the other two. If the winner is the warmest of the three, the reason must be specific to this subject, not "warm and friendly".
